solution_steps:
We can use long division to divide $7x^3 + 3x^2 - 5x - 8$ by $x + 2$:
$$
\begin{array}{c|cc cc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{7x^2} & -11x & +17 \\
\cline{2-5}
x+2 & 7x^3 & +3x^2 & -5x & -8 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{7x^3} & +14x^2 & & \\
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & -11x^2 & -5x & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & -11x^2 & -22x & \\
\cline{3-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 17x & -8 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 17x & +34 \\
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & -42 \\
\end{array}
$$
The quotient is $7x^2 - 11x + 17$ and the remainder is $-42$.
Therefore, the quotient when $7x^3 + 3x^2 - 5x - 8$ is divided by $x + 2$ is $\boxed{7x^2 - 11x + 17}$.The answer is: 7x^2-11x+17

